notes.body:
Templates use Go templating: {{ .Values.x }} inserts values, {{- if }} / {{- range }} control structure, and the leading dash trims whitespace. Worked example — values.yaml: ingress: {enabled: true, host: shop.example.com}, ports: [80, 443]. Template snippet: '{{- if .Values.ingress.enabled }}
host: {{ .Values.ingress.host }}
{{- end }}
{{- range .Values.ports }}
- containerPort: {{ . }}
{{- end }}'. Predict the render: 'host: shop.example.com' then '- containerPort: 80' and '- containerPort: 443'. Solution verification: the if is true so the host line renders; range iterates twice, '.' is each port. If enabled were false, the host line vanishes entirely. The professional habit: never helm install blind — run helm template ./chart --values prod-values.yaml and READ the rendered manifests first. Template errors (bad indentation, nil pointer on missing values) are caught here, not in production.

items.prompt:
values: {env: prod}. Template: '{{- if eq .Values.env "prod" }}
replicas: 5
{{- else }}
replicas: 1
{{- end }}'. Render?
